{
  "case_id": "2010-10-290",
  "document_hash": "3f974d7d6a34f70fe6d0791cc1cf160839505bc81eef8fa53aa249db74cdcad2",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Microsoft Corporation",
      "case_id": "2010-10-290",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f974d7d6a34f70fe6d0791cc1cf160839505bc81eef8fa53aa249db74cdcad2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f974d7d6a34-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Federal Circuit's clear and convincing\nevidence standard ensures the enforcement of invalid\npatents, even though this Court recognized in KSR that\ninvalid patents stifle rather than promote the progress\nof liberal arts. Under this Court's decisions Grogan\nand Huddleston, the default preponderance standard\nshould govern in all cases because section 282 does not\nspecify a heightened standard of proof."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-10-290",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f974d7d6a34f70fe6d0791cc1cf160839505bc81eef8fa53aa249db74cdcad2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f974d7d6a34-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: It would be hard to\nargue, Mr. Hungar, that it makes no sense, but it made"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-10-290",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f974d7d6a34f70fe6d0791cc1cf160839505bc81eef8fa53aa249db74cdcad2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f974d7d6a34-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If the challenger has the burden of persuasion, wouldn't it almost go without saying that the challenger would also have the burden of production on the issue of invalidity? So what would be added then by -- what role is played then by that sentence, a patent shall be presumed valid?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-10-290",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f974d7d6a34f70fe6d0791cc1cf160839505bc81eef8fa53aa249db74cdcad2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f974d7d6a34-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the court in RCA said a patent is presumed to be valid until the presumption has been overcome by convincing evidence of error."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-10-290",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f974d7d6a34f70fe6d0791cc1cf160839505bc81eef8fa53aa249db74cdcad2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f974d7d6a34-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, the problem with your argument, assuming its validity, is why do you need the second sentence? If Congress was intending to sweep up in the use of the word \"presumption\" the need to overturn it by clear and convincing evidence, why did you need the second sentence saying that the other side now bore the burden of persuasion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Microsoft",
      "case_id": "2010-10-290",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f974d7d6a34f70fe6d0791cc1cf160839505bc81eef8fa53aa249db74cdcad2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f974d7d6a34-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think there is a belt and suspenders quality to the statute, no matter how you parse it, but I think that Microsoft has essentially the"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-10-290",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f974d7d6a34f70fe6d0791cc1cf160839505bc81eef8fa53aa249db74cdcad2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f974d7d6a34-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Why is -- why is re-examination sufficient to answer the concerns that"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-10-290",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f974d7d6a34f70fe6d0791cc1cf160839505bc81eef8fa53aa249db74cdcad2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f974d7d6a34-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF THOMAS G. HUNGAR ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-10-290",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f974d7d6a34f70fe6d0791cc1cf160839505bc81eef8fa53aa249db74cdcad2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f974d7d6a34-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What about the rule where -- I'm trying this on, I don't buy it necessarily -- the -- the heightened standard exists where the Patent Office did consider it or could have considered it had the infringer asked for reconsideration?"
    },
